gBX(){return"Temperatures, rain, wind, sunshine, sun and moon times all come from Open-Meteo. The words, icons and advice are written by this app from those numbers, with fixed rules, so the same forecast always reads the same way."},
gBS(){return"A day in the Week list"},
gBR(){return"The icon and word come from the provider's weather type for each hour between 06:00 and 22:00, averaged: clear counts most, then mainly clear, partly cloudy, and cloudy least. A day where almost every hour is partly cloudy reads as partly cloudy, even if there are hours of sun in it, and one passing cloud does not turn a clear day cloudy. Rain or snow only decides the day when there are at least three wet hours in that time, or 3 mm in total, so one shower does not make a rainy day. Sunshine hours are shown separately."},
gBU(){return"An hour or a block of the day"},
gBT(){return"These use the weather type the provider gives for that hour, with its strength: light, plain or heavy rain, snow, drizzle and so on. A block (morning, noon, afternoon, evening, night) shows its most significant weather, so one hour of thunder makes it a thunder block. In daytime, an hour is lifted to a sunnier sky when the provider's own sunshine forecast for it is high (clear from 90 percent of the hour, mostly sunny from 70, partly cloudy from 40), because thin high cloud can make a cloud-based weather type look greyer than the sky really is. It is never made gloomier."},
